          <article class="card-list-text">
            <h2>Is Your Current Website ADA Compliant?</h2>
            <p>Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) is a federal law requiring you to design and develop a website accessible to people with disabilities, including those who are blind, deaf, or have limited mobility. Here at our web design agency in Los Angeles, we believe everyone deserves equal access to information and resources on the internet. That's why we'll invest lots of effort to ensure your website meets various <a href="/wordpress-ada-compliance-website">WordPress ADA compliance</a> requirements. Some of the best practices our web design experts follow include: </p>
          </article>
          <article class="card-list-cards">
            <div class="card-list-card">
                <p><strong>Using semantic HTML:</strong> Instead of using tags solely for formatting purposes, we use HTML tags that accurately describe the content on the page. This makes it easier for screen readers and other assistive technologies to understand and navigate the content on your website.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card-list-card">
                <p><strong>Providing alternative text for images:</strong> We'll include a short description for every image on your website, which will help screen readers describe visual elements to users who are blind or have low vision.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card-list-card">
                <p><strong>Using descriptive link text:</strong> By writing descriptive link texts, we'll make sure both users and assistive technologies get enough context to understand where each link points.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card-list-card">
                <p><strong>Adjustable font sizes and color schemes:</strong> Besides choosing the perfect font size and adjusting the contrast for maximum readability, we'll also implement features that allow visitors to adjust these elements. This way, everyone will be able to explore your website in the way they find most enjoyable.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card-list-card">
                <p><strong>Testing your website with assistive technologies:</strong> During the design process, our web design company in Los Angeles uses tools such as screen readers and keyboard navigation to test the accessibility of your website. This allows us to identify any potential issues early on and fix them on time.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card-list-card">
                <p><strong>Following web accessibility guidelines and standards:</strong> Alpha Efficiency's web design experts follow web accessibility guidelines and standards, such as WCAG, to ensure your website is accessible to everyone.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card-list-card">
                <p>In addition to being the right thing to do, ADA compliance is important from legal and SEO perspectives. If it's not accessible to people with disabilities, your website might face penalties from search engines. We can help you protect your business and ensure all users have an equally great experience on your website.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card-list-card">
                <article class="card-list-img">
                    <img src="/assets/images/locations-la/Img 168.webp" alt="ADA">
                </article>
            </div>
          </article>
          
    </div>
</section>

